        "original_id": "83a4890c-6ca9-55c0-b880-7304c8be784e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Kazanjian, Harry Kizirian, Chris Enss, Roy Rogers, Dale Evans\n- Organizations: Lucasfilm, United States Marine Corps\n- Roles: film producer, vice president, non-fiction author, writer\n- Topics: World War II, women in the Old West\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Kizirian was born on July 13, 1925, and he was an Armenian American member of the United States Marine Corps who served during World War II.\n- Howard G. Kazanjian was born on July 26, 1942, and he is an American film producer known for \"Raiders of the Lost Ark\" and \"Return of the Jedi.\"\n- Howard Kazanjian served for eight years as a Vice President of Lucasfilm, and he is also a published non-fiction author.\n- Chris Enss has written more than 20 books about women in the Old West.\n- Chris Enss collaborated with producer Howard Kazanjian on four books, including two about Roy Rogers and Dale Evans.\n- Harry Kizirian died on September 13, 2002.",
